# In-app notifications only

Never use native browser dialogs for user-facing messages in this project:

- Do **not** use `alert()`, `confirm()`, or `prompt()`.
- Do **not** add fallbacks to `window.alert` when a toast/modal helper is unavailable.

Use the existing UI instead:

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Short success/error/info | `VarydianUtils.showToast(message, type)` |
| Blocking OK dialog | `window.modalSystem.alert(title, message, options)` |
| Confirm before action | `window.modalSystem.confirm(...)` or an in-app modal |
| Destructive confirm | In-app modal with explicit Confirm/Cancel buttons |

When touching notification code, migrate any remaining `alert()` calls to the helpers above.

Admin and upload flows already use `VarydianUtils.showToast` — follow that pattern.
